[Music]  you  [Music]  whether you're brand new to the series  or just a little rusty Mario Kart 8  deluxe can be sort of intimidating it's  a cute racing game but it has the  potential to make you rage harder than  you ever knew you could so if you want  to destroy your enemies and all of your  friends here's what you tips the game  doesn't really tell you make sure to  subscribe so you don't miss any more  Mario Kart first things first you  probably know how to accelerate and  steer but if you really want to start  racing you gotta know how to boost to  get a boost at the start of a race press  and hold a as the countdown fades from 2  you do it too late you'll get a tinier  boost but if you're too early you'll  totally stall during the race press R  when you're going off a jump or ramp to  get a boost but if you're going too fast  into a turn don't be afraid to break so  you don't go flying off the track you  can also press X to check what's behind  you it's useful for seeing who or what  is coming your way note that two new  settings Auto steer and Auto accelerate  are on by default so if you're not into  that be sure to turn them off before you  start once you've gotten the hang of  driving it's time to drift this one  takes some practice your main goal is to  turn as tightly and quickly as possible  to keep your time low and prevent  yourself from flying off the track and  the longer you drift the better your  speed boost will be when you let go  you'll see sparks flying off your cart  when and where you should begin drifting  depends on your car configuration which  we'll get to in a bit but as a general  rule of thumb for carts at least start  drifting right before the curved part of  the track starts bikes have much better  handling than carts and require a  lighter touch so if you're new to  drifting I recommend starting out on  carts first to get a feel for it  once you've played a bit you'll probably  have a fair amount of coins you can  collect up to ten each race don't ignore  them because they go toward unlocking  cart parts and car customization really  matters carts have five stats speed  acceleration weight handling and  traction press the plus or minus button  to see stats in the cart selection  screen the first two are pretty  self-explanatory the speed stat  indicates your top speed while  acceleration is how quickly you gain  speed and therefore recover from getting  hit or falling off the track weight is  what it sounds like in carts with a  higher weight can knock away those with  lower weights handling dictates how  sharp a turn you can make and is really  important for tougher tracks and higher  difficulties and note that bikes have  higher handling than carts and make much  sharper turns finally traction is how  well your car can grip the road and it  can help keep you from slowing down too  much on off-road terrain experiment with  different kart fields to find one that  works for you I prefer high top speed  middle acceleration and high handling  over anything else these stats are  partially affected by the character you  choose there are three main weight  classes light medium and heavy with a  bit of variation within them characters  like the baby's toad and dry bones are  light mid-sized characters like Mario  Peach Yoshi in the Inklings are medium  and larger and metal characters like  Rosalina Bowser Wario and pink gold  peach are heavy heavier characters have  higher top speeds but lower acceleration  handling and traction so tailor your  Kart to account for the character you  choose Nintendo's record best times on  the wii u version we're set with heavy  characters using the sport bike slick  wheels and parafoil glider for the most  part for right now I'm rocking the mid  weight inkling girl with the splat buggy  slick wheels and super glider and it's  working well for my style  I recommend testing out new kart configs  in the time trials mode to see which  setups get you the best times  once you've mastered the art of racing  it's time to unleash hell upon your  opponents  that's where items come in  you can use items with L but if you hold  L you can carry some items like bananas  and shells behind you if you're targeted  by a red or green shell they'll protect  you from getting hit just don't do it  with a BA bomb because it'll explode  if you're in first and you get a super  horn hold on to it it can knock away  items and other racers but it can also  protect you from the infamous blue shell  use it while the shell is hovering over  you to destroy it and everyone else's  hopes of winning even if you've unlocked  everything you could possibly want don't  ignore coins having 10 grants you a very  small top speed boost and it can mean  the difference between first and second  place finally when you get a mushroom  save it for shortcuts it'll help you  make it over grass or other weird  surfaces you can save a bunch of time if  you're curious about where the best  shortcuts are you're in luck because we  already have a handy video all about  them now that you're a master class  racer let us know in the comments what  other tips and tricks you stumble upon  thanks for watching  [Music]

